  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Triple match – three 1v1s at once",
  "description": "Three separate 1v1 games are played at the same time inside a small area with two small nets, about 15 × 10 metres (not to scale – the area is drawn larger so the players are easy to see). Each pair has its own puck. Whoever has the puck attacks, and the roles switch the moment the puck is won. With all three battles sharing the same space it gets crowded, so players keep meeting new 1v1 situations.\n\nAdjust the size: a smaller area means less time and more battles, a bigger one gives more time but easily turns into plain skating with the puck. With more players, set up two areas side by side.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Attack: fake one way and go the other – follow it up with a change of pace."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Attack: keep your body between the defender and the puck."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defence: skate backwards, facing the attacker and staying between them and the net, and steer them wide."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Ask the players: what do you need to think about attacking 1v1 – and defending?"
    }
  ],
